'' ABS OF AN UNSIGNED ARGUMENT IS STILL llabs. This used to refuse one, on the
'' reasoning that an unsigned value has nothing to take the absolute of -- but fbc
'' does it anyway, and measurably:
''
''   dim as ulong    a = abs( ul )    A$0 = (uint32)__builtin_llabs( (int64)UL$0 )
''   dim as ulongint b = abs( ull )   B$0 = __builtin_llabs( ULL$0 )
''
'' -- widened, llabs, narrowed back. Refusing left it to a path that has no answer for
'' ABS at all, so every one of them declined: optimizations/consteval.bas runs the
'' whole unary family over every width, and lost 13 statements to it.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/abs-unsigned.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: zext
'' EXPECT-OUT: iabs
'' GOLDEN: expected/abs-unsigned.out
